nts, taking Black's lead from +22.1 to +13.5, with E8 the engine's choice. Black stayed far ahead, so the slip didn't change the result."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script either read files, called choose_opponent/play with a hand-picked move, or ran inspect112/verify112, which parse the returned board, count groups, liberties and area, and replay only the moves actually played to check legality and captures. Nothing looped over empty points to score candidates or played sequences forward, and the move choices were made manually in the notes.", "stop": false}}